// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: an UN-ANNOTATED anonymous object literal (`const c = { r: n }`)
// assigned into a module GLOBAL annotated at a union ARM (`let gsto: Circle`), in a module
// that also declares a standalone struct of that arm's exact layout (`Dot`). Twelve lines,
// no import, no generic, no lambda, no list. `vl check` exits 0 — one redundant-annotation
// HINT, no error — and is the ONLY command that misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1,
// `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The message is the stable
// identifier, and the two `$type`s are two DIFFERENT heap types behind one placeholder.)
//
// IT IS D39's CHANNEL PROBLEM AT A DESTINATION THAT IS NOT A `return`. An anonymous
// `{ r: n }` has TWO nominal claimants — `structIndexOfObj` finds `Dot` by field set,
// `objVariantName` finds `Circle` by field set — and neither scan is wrong: delete `Dot`
// and the same program runs, so this cannot be fixed by reordering the ladder. Only the
// CONTEXT decides, and the context here is the assignment TARGET's annotation, which the
// literal never sees. `synthRetPinAnn` carries exactly this fact for the RETURN
// destination; a GLOBAL and a callee PARAM have no equivalent.
//
// THE `return n` AND THE TOP-LEVEL READ ARE LOAD-BEARING — checked, not assumed. Drop them
// and the same shape is a LOUD `emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape` instead,
// which is a different row. Run this file verbatim; a retyped minimisation measured the
// other program.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, not a regression: silent on master `a97c9ae1` too, with the same `vl check`
// rc 0 and the same engine message. It is `silent-class-inventory.md` D81, and it is 48 of
// the 116 cells the D52 grid leaves silent (the PARAM leg of the same root is the other 40).
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty.
// @hint redundant type annotation: `gsto` is inferred as `{r: i32}`
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }
let gsto: Circle = { r: 0 }
function mk(n: i32) {
  const c = { r: n }
  gsto = c
  return n
}
mk(7)
print((gsto).r)
